#: ../../source/docs/common-moving-vehicle-initialization.rst:5
#: cf5f6f48c8184e04ab81ecff6674f0b4
msgid "Moving Vehicle Initialization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-moving-vehicle-initialization.rst:7
#: 3a49337d3cc94c618fe8d282aff93f2e
msgid "ArduPilot allows taking off from a moving platform such as boats or other moving vehicles.  It is basically a change to how the gyros are calibrated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-moving-vehicle-initialization.rst:13
#: f1c10ac45e1545d88742682a498802c0
msgid "Settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-moving-vehicle-initialization.rst:15
#: fa14e81ba9d149eea0f211ff822bdacc
msgid "In many cases Copters, Rovers, and Planes will be able to take off from a moving platform without any special parameter changes as long as the platform is not moving too rapidly during the gyro calibration which occurs a few seconds after startup (look for the LEDs flashing red and blue)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-moving-vehicle-initialization.rst:17
#: dffb3b749ccc4e76b191d03c10b8b28c
msgid "If the platform is moving too much however, the gyro calibration will fail after 30 seconds and gyro related warnings like \"Bad Gyro Health\" will appear on the HUD.  Despite this warning the vehicle may fly normally but having the warning is unnerving and may hide other errors.  In this case, it is best to disable the automatic gyro calibration by setting the :ref:`INS_GYR_CAL <INS_GYR_CAL>` parameter to \"0\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-moving-vehicle-initialization.rst:20
#: aef202429eff402d98430b92cf9f0be8
msgid "Manually trigger gyro calibration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-moving-vehicle-initialization.rst:22
#: cb7f1ac1813b4b11ad1c5d96ab456628
msgid "Note that even with automatic gyro calibration disabled, the gyros calibration can be triggered manually from the Mission Planner (and perhaps some other ground stations) using the Flight Data screen's Actions tab.  Select \"PREFLIGHT_CALIBRATION\" from the top-left drop-down and then press the \"Do Action\" button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-moving-vehicle-initialization.rst:27
#: 2168afd4fd43466d952ccf97caaa10d4
msgid "This is useful if for some reason a gyro calibration is required and the vehicle can be temporarily placed on a near non-moving platform."
msgstr ""
